    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

<main class="wrap">

  <div class="view" id="view-home">
    <div class="row-top" id="about">
      <figure class="photo box" id="photo" aria-label="Photo of Eduardo Gallareta">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Eduardo Gallareta at the Tec Science Summit, Tecnológico de Monterrey" width="640" height="640">
      </figure>
      <section class="about box">
        <div class="label">About me</div>
        <h1>Eduardo Gallareta</h1>
        <p class="lede">Biotechnology Engineering student developing diagnostic and applied biotechnology tools at the intersection of microfluidics, synthetic biology, and artificial intelligence.</p>
        <div class="about-text">
          <p>I am an undergraduate student in Biotechnology Engineering at Tecnológico de Monterrey, where I have been enrolled since August 2024. My academic and research interests center on applied biotechnology, synthetic biology, molecular diagnostics, microfluidics, and data science, with particular emphasis on translating computational models into functional devices.</p>
          <p>I conduct research through independent projects, in collaboration with Healthen Group, and within Prometheus Research Department, a student research organization I have led as President since June 2026. I am currently seeking a semester-long research internship in a laboratory setting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="meta"><span>Monterrey, Mexico</span><span>President, Prometheus Research Department (June 2026 – present)</span></div>
        <div class="contact" id="contact">
          <span class="label">Contact</span>
          <div class="email">
            <code id="mail">lalo.gallareta@gmail.com</code>
            <button type="button" id="copy">Copy</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="cards">
      <a class="card box" href="#skills">
        <div class="top"><h2>Skills</h2><span class="num">05</span></div>
        <p>Computational and wet-lab methods used across my projects.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Machine learning · PyTorch</li>
          <li>Molecular dynamics · GROMACS, COMSOL</li>
          <li>Cheminformatics · molecular biology</li>
        </ul>
        <span class="go">View skills →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card box" href="#research">
        <div class="top"><h2>Research</h2><span class="num">07</span></div>
        <p>Biosensing, microfluidics, generative AI for molecules, and synthetic biology.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Hindered protein transport in hydrogels</li>
          <li>Microfluidic lab-on-chip for ctDNA</li>
          <li>Generative design of biosurfactants</li>
        </ul>
        <span class="go">View projects →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card box" href="#publications">
        <div class="top"><h2>Publications</h2><span class="num">04</span></div>
        <p>First-author, co-author, and collaborating contributions, 2026.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>IEEE conference manuscript (first author)</li>
          <li>IEEE CBMS 2026 · MicroClinic</li>
          <li>Frontiers in Nutrition · CIDPRO</li>
        </ul>
        <span class="go">View publications →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="view" id="view-research" hidden>
    <a class="back" href="#home">← Home</a>
    <div class="view-title"><h2>Research</h2><span class="label">7 projects · 2024 – present</span></div>
    <div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects by area">
          <button type="button" id="f-all" data-f="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
          <button type="button" id="f-ia" data-f="ia" aria-pressed="false">AI</button>
          <button type="button" id="f-micro" data-f="micro" aria-pressed="false">Microfluidics</button>
          <button type="button" id="f-bio" data-f="bio" aria-pressed="false">Synthetic biology</button>
          <button type="button" id="f-sim" data-f="sim" aria-pressed="false">Modeling &amp; simulation</button>
          <button type="button" id="f-dx" data-f="dx" aria-pressed="false">Diagnostics</button>
        </div>
        <div class="projects">

          <article class="proj" data-tags="sim dx">
            <div class="when">2026<span class="role">First author</span></div>
            <div>
              <h3>Hindered Protein Transport in Nanoporous Hydrogels for Biosensing</h3>
              <div class="org">Healthen Group</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Developed a continuum framework for hindered protein transport (myoglobin and C-reactive protein) in nanoporous hydrogels, incorporating steric hindrance models (Dechadilok–Deen, Renkin), lognormal pore-size distributions, and sensitivity analysis.</li>
                <li>Introduced a methodological distinction between flux-referred (D<sub>eff</sub>) and storage-corrected (D<sub>lag</sub>) diffusivities, preventing a 1/S overestimation of the membrane time lag (approximately threefold for CRP).</li>
                <li>Performed molecular dynamics simulations in GROMACS (AMBER99SB-ILDN, SPC/E water, 310 K, 20 ns) with Yeh–Hummer finite-size corrections as consistency checks on diffusion coefficients.</li>
